# Changelog

## [0.19.2] - 2026-01-16

### Added
- monitor: reaper for orphan tasks

### Fixed
- monitor/cli: dead workers reaper and removed old command
- monitor/reaper: handle access denied to pid we don't own

## [0.19.1] - 2025-11-05

### Added
- cli/monitor: --pinned option for host filtering
- worker: direct rework-worker entrypoint to bypass click overhead

### Changed
- monitor: removed host filter to allow distributed execution
- notification: include domain in channel names
- notify: use cn.notify() for safe identifier quoting
- packaging: migrated metadata to pyproject.toml

### Fixed
- monitor: cross-domain notification issue
- test/monitor: intermittent failure
- test: reduced delays and faster teardown
- helper/host: silenced warning

## [0.19.0] - 2025-08-29

### Added
- monitor: stopping flag for clean shutdown
- initial LISTEN/NOTIFY implementation

### Changed
- replaced sqlalchemy with sqlhelp throughout
- sqlhelp: use binary protocol
- tests: postgresql cluster handling moved to sqlhelp
- schema: follow changes in sqlhelp
- helper/setlogger: register only once

### Fixed
- removed all remnants of sqlalchemy/psycopg2

## [0.18.0] - 2025-02-27

### added
- custom vacuum rules per operation (#3)
- vacuum parameters exposed in monitor (rework_ui#10)

### changed
- simplified schema initialization

### fixed
- cli/init-db to follow schema constructor change
- removed spurious [y/n] block in unregister-operation command (#12)

## [0.17.2] - 2024-10-25

### fixed
- cli/vacuum with --tasks --queued now correctly preserves queued tasks
- moved CI to heptapod
- silenced ruff deprecation warnings

## [0.17.1] - 2024-08-23

### fixed
- step() scheduling when defined by web-ui
- argument passing between prepared call and actual invocation, correcting domain dispatch

## [0.17.0] - 2024-03-07

### added
- io default values support
- helper/next_stamps_from_cronrules: low-level primitive for cron scheduling
- cli/scheduled-plan: command to list next hour schedules for a domain
- monitor schedule plan in logs
- next scheduled run time indication
- better logging infrastructure with debug support

### changed
- replaced apscheduler with icron (croniter successor)
- monitor uses logging instead of print statements
- improved scheduler logging and crash handling
- better segregation of log messages by origin
- switched to bookworm/postgres 15 in CI

### fixed
- task/join handling of 'running' target
- api/prepare provides empty dict when spec exists but no input given
- scheduler step re-initializes runnable list
- made max_mem test more robust

## [0.16.0] - 2024-02-14

### added
- cli/vacuum --domain option (defaults to "default")
- pytype static type checking
- __version__ attribute in package root
- io/boolean input type for convenience
- tox for test running

### changed
- tasks/capturelogs forces flush at std flush time
- deprecated sync parameter in capturelog, removed threaded flush

### removed
- deprecated input module

### fixed
- blocked sqlalchemy major version incompatibility
- various linter cleanups

## [0.15.1] - 2024-01-10

### changed
- cli/vacuum uses --days parameter instead of --finished for convenience

## [0.15.0] - 2023-12-15

### added
- helper/prepared function to get pre-scheduled tasks and payloads

### fixed
- scheduler now avoids overlapping scheduling of same tasks
- better indication of ambiguous operations in api

## [0.14.0] - 2022-01-13

### added
- sourcehut CI build spec
- type validation for api/prepare input data
- helper/convert_io to convert strings to types for prepare/schedule calls
- more information shown for abort case in cli/list-tasks

### changed
- switched from zstd to pyzstd (provides binary packages)
- improved test robustness for scheduler timing effects

### fixed
- api/prepare detection for non-existing operation/domain
- api/prepare crashes on bad input with proper type validation
- helper/neary_unpack bad exception type
- various format to f-string conversions

## [0.13.0] - 2021-09-21

### added
- cli/unregister-operation command with color output
- initial support for spec-ed outputs handling in api and schema
- task state construction factoring for reuse
- helper functions for file handling in packed io blocks
- protection against duplicate schedule plans in api/prepare

### changed
- scheduler forbids "every second" rule by default for safety
- cli/list-operations shows domain and reorders attributes
- moved inputs.py to io.py (inputs and outputs handling)
- api/prepare takes empty input if there is one (avoid None vs {} issues)
- outputs validation ensures only valid spec-ed output can be saved

### deprecated
- rework/input module (use io module instead)

### fixed
- cli/new_worker debug_port detection
- api/prepare protection against duplicate inputs
- cli/unregister-operation interaction logic

## [0.12.0] - 2022-12-26

### added
- scheduler with extended cron format including seconds support
- inputs specification system for task operations (bytes, int, float, str, datetime)
- automatic input marshalling/unmarshalling with zstd compression
- moment input type accepting lisp expressions for dates
- cli/list-scheduled command for scheduled operations
- cli/scheduler export/import functionality for schedule migration
- api/prepare endpoint for handling input specification protocol

### changed
- dropped python 2 compatibility completely
- replaced .format calls with f-strings throughout codebase
- scheduler loop runs for each monitor step
- better input validation and error handling

### fixed
- index name conflicts in schema
- list-operations command parameter shifting
- variable capture bug in monitor/scheduler

### removed
- setup.cfg (pure python 3 builds only)

## [0.11.1] - 2022-10-11

### fixed
- repository uri in package metadata
- missing import in cli/init-db command

## [0.11.0] - 2022-06-23

### added
- signal handling for monitor (TERM signal)
- configurable timeout for task start limit
- asynchronous worker startup tracking to prevent monitor crashes

### changed
- task/capturelog sync option defaults to True for safer operation
- improved worker startup timeout handling
- better pylint compliance across modules

### fixed
- timedelta.total_seconds usage (was incorrectly using microseconds)
- schema status type namespace issues
- various python 2 compatibility removals

## [0.10.1] - 2021-09-21

### fixed
- race condition in helper/cpu_usage (psutil.Process.cpu_percent crashes)
- monitor crash when reaping dead workers
- simplified monitor run/step loop

## [0.10.0] - 2021-09-21

### added
- monitor --debugfile switch for tracking monitor crashes
- api/workers context manager for on-the-spot monitor+workers allocation
- task accessor for worker death info
- monitor step() method extraction
- monitor cleanup method
- task abortion marking under specific conditions

### changed
- worker converted to class-based architecture
- monitor extracts step method for maintenance operations
- better task status reporting for killed tasks

### fixed
- monitor exception handling for aborted tasks
- task property values are transaction scoped

## [0.9.3] - 2020-12-11

### fixed
- resource tracker helpers issues
- packaging marked as not zip-safe due to sql files

## [0.9.2] - 2020-09-04

### fixed
- race condition in helper/cpu_usage with psutil.Process.cpu_percent

## [0.9.1] - 2020-07-03

### added
- tox.ini configuration file
- documentation updates for newer vocabulary

### changed
- use psycopg2 binary distribution

### fixed
- missing sqlhelp dependency
- missing sql file in package

## [0.9.0] - 2020-07-02

### added
- cpu usage tracking for workers and process trees
- instant cpu usage monitoring

### changed
- replaced sqlalchemy with sqlhelp for database operations
- improved task log handling without assertions on root handlers

### fixed
- api/schedule host selection logic (try without host first)
- task/logs removal of root handler assertions

## [0.8.0] - 2019-11-20

### added
- config file support via REWORKCFGPATH environment variable
- sphinx documentation skeleton with api and test utilities sections
- task/worker timestamps (queued/started, created/started/finished)
- static timeout parameter on operations
- helper.utcnow usage for correct timestamps

### changed
- cli/deploy renamed to cli/monitor for better terminology
- task queued/started timestamp distinction
- api/task entry point sanity checks
- api/schedule function signature cleanup

### fixed
- python 2 compatibility issues
- missing inireader dependency

## [0.7.0] - 2019-09-18

### added
- task finished datetime attribute
- asynchronous log capture by default for better performance
- memory tracking moved to monitor (no maintenance thread in worker)
- maxruns handling logic extraction for testing

### changed
- helper/host stops doing name lookups (performance improvement)
- stdout/stderr linefeed handling in task capture
- monitor cleanup of unstarted workers with quantity reporting

### fixed
- stdout/stderr linefeed handling when captured
- dummy flush method on PGLogWriter for stdout compatibility
- domain handling for maxruns > 1
- space handling in helper/logs
- log flushing at end of tasks

## [0.6.0] - 2019-07-16

### added
- cli plugin override capability for standard commands
- operations info object for monitor event tracking
- cli/register-operations command with domain/asdomain support
- transaction support across operations

### changed
- test requirements moved to extra_requires
- worker abortion delegated to monitor for locked worker situations
- extracted worker list cleanup logic
- improved minworker test robustness

### fixed
- worker shutdown candidate selection (avoid double scheduling)
- monitor debugging output improvements

## [0.5.0] - 2019-01-11

### added
- explicit database representation of monitor
- cli/list-monitors command

### fixed
- task/logs PGLogHandler removal safety (handles wiped logging handlers)

## [0.4.0] - 2018-11-16

### added
- Monitor object architecture replacing function-based approach
- minworkers parameter for worker scaling
- cautious worker rampdown approach to reach minworkers

### changed
- monitor immediate handling of worker count
- monitor directly handles workers with better responsibility
- improved worker lifecycle management and timing

### fixed
- better domain-specific worker kill prevention
- racy assertions in worker count monitoring
- worker shrinking detection on non-unix systems

## [0.3.0] - 2018-10-05

### added
- domain map support for operation recording to renamed domains
- task scheduling on specific domains
- debugport configuration in database entities
- proper debugport number recycling in monitor

### changed
- moved running status manager out of worker main loop
- reorganized worker heartbeat code
- immediate disposal of Popen objects with zombie reaper

### fixed
- proper handling/recycling of debugport numbers
- subprocess stdout/stderr stream handling

## [0.2.0] - 2018-07-02

### added
- extensible cli command system for third-party components
- cli/list-operations subcommand
- task.join method for coordination routines (1s polling)
- cli/shutdown-worker and cli/kill-worker commands
- cli/vacuum command to clean old tasks and workers
- debugging support with pystuck (optional)
- raw input/output data support for tasks
- domain concept with multi-domain worker management

### changed
- made rework command extensible through plugins
- improved max_runs handling to be properly honored
- better worker kill handling outside transaction context
- monitor safety belt for worker startup time

### fixed
- maxruns argument not being honored
- preemptive kill signaling from monitor to worker
- locking issues in monitor
- cli test reporting for killed worker tasks

## [0.1.0] - 2017-11-09

### added
- initial operation/task/worker/monitor system (postgresql/sqlalchemy based)
- operation registry for out-of-process function name/module communication
- uniform task api with self-regulating worker/monitor
- worker shutdown signaling mechanism with traceback field
- preemptive task abortion with signal through database
- dead worker detection by monitor with live-check
- task log capture (stdout/stderr/logging) with context manager
- total ordering in database matching log emission order
- task input property and Task.fromqueue classmethod
- cli/list-workers command showing status and current tasks
- cli/list-tasks command with status, traceback, log lines
- cli/tasklog command to show logs for given task
- cli/abort-task command for task termination
- worker memory usage tracking
- task synthetic state property (queued/running/aborting/failed/done)
- task creation datetime field
- worker maxruns option for automatic shutdown
- worker maxmem option for memory limit enforcement
- task metadata field (json) for flexible app-related storage
- schema with proper indexes on foreign key columns
- python 2 compatibility support
- advanced operation management towards distributedness
- task error handling with traceback capture without worker penalties
- monitor detection of dead workers from hard crashes
- recycled worker pid detection heuristics
- task status reporting after sudden worker death
